## AI Agent Reasoning

### Context
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md and a prior gap-analysis spec
(specs/habit-tracker-v2-specifications.md, already present in the working
tree from a previous session) both identified the same root problem: all
the habit-tracker React components and the useHabits hook were built and
unit-tested in isolation, but the actual /habits route rendered a
completely separate, hand-written vanilla-JS CRUD list. This was the
highest-impact gap since it made ~500 lines of tested component code
unreachable by real users and left the core spec'd UX (scrollable table +
synced calendar + legend) entirely missing from the running app.

### Decisions Made
- Composition root as a plain component (HabitApp.tsx) rather than putting
  all logic directly in the island wrapper: keeps the island itself a thin,
  untestable-but-trivial shim (mirroring the existing game island pattern)
  while HabitApp can be rendered directly in vitest without any DOM-mounting
  machinery.
- Legend filtering uses 'isolate on click' semantics (clicking a habit in
  the legend shows only that habit, clicking again restores 'show all')
  rather than a plain per-habit toggle set that starts empty. This matches
  the spec's 'toggles visibility ... across both views' language while
  giving a more useful default interaction for a legend with many habits.
- Removed Space Invaders entirely rather than leaving it dormant: since
  root already redirected to /habits and no route pointed at /game, the
  entire game module (routes, templates, TS engine, tests, e2e) was dead
  code with zero external reachability. Deleting it removes maintenance
  burden without any behavior change for real users.
- Fixed the duplicate Alembic migration heads (9b1c2d3e4f5a and
  f1a2b3c4d5e6 both had down_revision = e31396db40b1) by rechaining rather
  than merging: a linear chain (hello -> habits/entries -> drop hello) is
  simpler to reason about than an Alembic merge revision, and there was no
  reason for the two migrations to be independent branches — this was a
  straightforward oversight (two migrations authored against the same base
  without rebasing), not an intentional branch.
- Fixed frontend typecheck/lint (pre-existing failures on every test file,
  not introduced by this change) via ambient type declarations placed
  inside src/ (test-globals.d.ts) rather than adding @types/node, since the
  project does not otherwise depend on Node types and only needs the single
  ambient 'global' identifier used by fetch-stubbing tests.

### Trade-offs
- Implemented only a single-level Ctrl/Cmd+Z undo (re-toggle last cell)
  rather than a full undo/redo stack with Shift+Arrow range selection and
  bulk-marking, which the original spec also calls for. These are
  documented as the next-highest-priority remaining gaps in
  IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md rather than attempted in this pass, to keep this
  increment focused and fully verified (unit + integration + e2e) rather
  than partially implementing several large interaction features at once.
- e2e tests generate random hex colors per run (icon+color uniqueness is
  enforced server-side) rather than resetting the dev database between
  runs, since there was no existing test-database-reset tooling in the
  repo and adding one was out of scope for this increment.

